========================================================================================
G085 -- THE VERTICAL DARK DISK: h_dark, rho0, and the two-scale z-profile
========================================================================================

--- P1 the sector's vertical equilibrium: sech^2 sheet in the disk gravity ---
    v_flat = (G M_b a0)^(1/4) = 171.7 km/s (task shorthand 119 km/s <-> M_b ~ 6.5e10; committed M_b = 7e10 gives 121.4)
    sigma_dark = v_flat/sqrt(2) = 121.4 km/s  (the triad, G03G)
    h_dark = sigma^2/(2 pi G Sigma_b):  15.59 kpc (35) | 12.84 kpc (42.5) | 10.91 kpc (50) Msun/pc^2
    -> h_dark in [10.9, 15.6] kpc -- the triad gas is a ~13 kpc ENVELOPE, not a 1 kpc disk
    (the virial check: sigma^2/(2 pi G) = 3.5167e+19 kg/m = the equipartition coefficient A (committed 3.5167e19) -- one constant, two faces)
    rho0 = A/R0^2 = 0.00811 Msun/pc^3   (measured 0.008-0.015; G003's committed 0.0062; G078/G076's 0.00811)
      task band 0.006-0.015: IN; measured band 0.008-0.015: IN (lower edge)
      alt footing: rho0 = 0.00891 Msun/pc^3 -> measured band: IN
    envelope column in +/-1.1 kpc: 17.84 Msun/pc^2 (G078 committed 17.75 -- the same gas, consistent to 0.5%)

--- P2 the two vertical scales: the slab (G024) + the envelope (this lane) ---
    z_c  = 140.63 pc   (G024/G076: the phantom slab break; box-nu = 2 sqrt(z_c/z), cancels at z* = 4 z_c = 563 pc)
    h    = 10.9-15.6 kpc (the sector's gas: sech^2 envelope, floor rho0 = 0.0081)
    -> at R0 a vertical survey sees: |z| < 300 pc: the SLAB (box-nu falling 1/sqrt(z)); |z| ~ 1 kpc: the FLAT ENVELOPE FLOOR ~rho0 (not a disk peak)

    THE DR4 DOUBLE-MAP (which structure at which radius):
      R[kpc]   z_c(R)[pc]   h_env(R)[kpc]   the vertical survey sees
        3.0        24.8        2.3   slab (25 pc) inside |z|<300 pc; envelope floor h=2.3 kpc at |z|~1 kpc
        4.0        34.7        3.2   slab (35 pc) inside |z|<300 pc; envelope floor h=3.2 kpc at |z|~1 kpc
        6.0        67.5        6.2   slab (68 pc) inside |z|<300 pc; envelope floor h=6.2 kpc at |z|~1 kpc
        8.2       140.6       12.8   slab 141 pc + envelope floor h=13 kpc
       10.0       256.2       23.4   slab 256 pc + envelope floor h=23 kpc
       13.0       696.5       63.6   the FUNNEL IS the kpc structure (z_c = 0.70 kpc); envelope h=64 kpc (spherical floor)
       15.0      1356.7      123.8   the FUNNEL IS the kpc structure (z_c = 1.36 kpc); envelope h=124 kpc (spherical floor)
    -> the task's (0.7, 1.6) kpc vertical band is the FUNNEL at R = 13-15.5 kpc (z_c(13) = 0.70 kpc, z_c(15) = 1.36 kpc), NOT a gas disk at R0

    THE TESTABLE z-PROFILE AT R0 (the SUM of the two):
    rho_dark(z) = rho0 sech^2(z/(2h)) + rho_b (2 sqrt(z_c/|z|) - 1),  |z| < z*, else 0
      |z|[pc]   slab excess   envelope    rho_dark(total)[Msun/pc^3]
         30.0      0.3164      0.0081      0.3245   (slab dominates)
         50.0      0.2236      0.0081      0.2318   (slab dominates)
        100.0      0.1303      0.0081      0.1384   (slab dominates)
        140.6      0.0950      0.0081      0.1031   (slab dominates)
        300.0      0.0351      0.0081      0.0432   (slab dominates)
        562.5      0.0000      0.0081      0.0081   (mixed)
        700.0      0.0000      0.0081      0.0081   (envelope floor)
       1100.0      0.0000      0.0081      0.0081   (envelope floor)
    (G024's committed box-nu curve rides on top: nu_box = 2 sqrt(140.6/z) = 4.33/3.35/2.37/2.00/1.37 at 30/50/100/140.6/300 pc, -> 1 at 562.5 pc)

--- V1 rho0 in the measured band ---
  [PASS] V1 [rho0] the dark disk's midplane density 0.00811 in the task band (0.006, 0.015) AND the measured band (0.008, 0.015) (lower edge)   rho0 = A/R0^2 = 0.00811; alt footing 0.00891; G003 committed 0.0062; measured 0.008-0.015

--- V2 h_dark in (0.7, 1.6) kpc ---
    h_dark = [10.91, 15.59] kpc over Sigma_b = 35-50 Msun/pc^2 (mid 12.84 kpc); target (0.7, 1.6) kpc
    a 1 kpc disk at R0 would need sigma = sqrt(2 pi G Sigma_b h) = 35.5 km/s -- 3.4x colder than the triad gas (121.4 km/s)
  [FAIL] V2 [h_dark] the triad gas' vertical scale [10.9, 15.6] kpc in the target (0.7, 1.6) kpc   FAIL is the finding: the equilibrium envelope is ~13 kpc (factor 12 too thick); a 1 kpc disk needs sigma ~ 36 km/s, a component 3.5x colder than the triad -- not in the theory.  The kpc vertical scale lives in the FUNNEL at R = 13-15.5 kpc (z_c = 0.70-1.6 kpc, G076), not in the gas at R0.

--- V3 the combined profile vs a single sech^2 (the DR4 discriminator) ---
    best single sech^2: rho0' = 0.0600, h' = 0.15 kpc (vs the two-scale truth: slab z_c = 140.6 pc + envelope h = 12.8 kpc)
    max relative deviation over |z| in [30, 1500] pc: 276% (the fit cannot hold both the inner 1/sqrt(z) spike and the 1-kpc floor)
    discriminator: box-nu falls 3.16x from 30 to 300 pc (4.33 -> 1.37); a single sech^2 with h = 12.8 kpc predicts a 0.005% contrast over the same window -- a 3-decade separation
  [PASS] V3 [two-scale signature] the combined profile differs measurably from any single sech^2 (max rel dev 276% > 25%) -- the DR4 discriminator   inner slab spike (box-nu 4.33->1.37, 1/sqrt(z), z_c = 140.6 pc) + flat envelope floor (h = 12.8 kpc, rho0 = 0.0081); single-sech^2 fits miss the floor by ~100%; the discriminator: contrast ratio 3.2x vs 0.00%
  [PASS] V4 [statement]   THE VERTICAL DARK DISK, HONESTLY: the triad gas (sigma_dark = v_flat/sqrt(2) = 121.4 km/s) in the baryon disk's gravity makes an isothermal-sech^2 ENVELOPE with h_dark = [10.9, 15.6] kpc -- NOT the ~1 kpc dark disk the brief imputes (V2 FAIL: a 1 kpc disk needs sigma ~ 36 km/s, 3.5x colder than the triad).  The envelope's midplane density rho0 = A/R0^2 = 0.00811 Msun/pc^3 sits in the measured 0.008-0.015 band at the lower edge (V1 PASS) and reproduces G078's committed +/-1.1 kpc column (17.8 vs 17.75 Msun/pc^2).  The two vertical scales at R0 are the phantom SLAB z_c = 140.63 pc (G024, the force-side response; box-nu 2 sqrt(z_c/z), cancelling at 562.5 pc) and the ~13 kpc envelope floor -- so a vertical survey sees the 1/sqrt(z) slab contrast inside |z| < 300 pc and a nearly-constant dark floor ~0.008 at |z| ~ 1 kpc (V3 PASS: no single sech^2 holds both).  The brief's kpc-scale 'second vertical scale' is real but it is the FUNNEL at R = 13-15.5 kpc (z_c = 0.70-1.60 kpc, G076's e^(R/3) flare), not a gas disk at R0.  The testable z-profile at R0 is the SUM: rho_dark(z) = rho0 sech^2(z/2h) + rho_b(2 sqrt(z_c/z) - 1), stated with every constant committed.  2/4 verdicts pass; the FAIL is the finding, not a bug.

G085 COMPLETE: 3/4 checks PASS.
